-- ============================================================================
-- DR11 EXPERT DEEP SEED: Well Integrity & P&A, advanced tier.
--
-- Six modules, 26 lessons, 132 questions. The structure row is GENERATED from
-- the tier's manifest.json rather than hand typed.
--
-- What this tier owns: taking the well permanently out of service. Balanced
-- plug placement, the permanent barrier rules, annular cement, and the
-- abandonment programme.
--
-- EVERY RULE HERE IS A PROXY FOR EVIDENCE YOU CANNOT GET ONCE THE RIG HAS
-- LEFT. A length stands in for a seal you cannot retest, a foundation stands
-- in for a plug that cannot fall, a log stands in for cement you cannot see.
--
-- THE RESULT THAT SURPRISES EVERYONE, AND IT IS NOT ABOUT EXCESS. The plug
-- ends up DEEPER than the balanced column suggests, and it does so EVEN AT
-- ZERO EXCESS. While the stinger is in the hole the slurry stands in the
-- annulus PLUS the stinger bore, which together are about 91 percent of the
-- full hole; pull the stinger and the same slurry redistributes across the
-- wider bore, so the top drops. On the published fixture it drops 15.365 m
-- with no excess at all. THE ANCHOR: at zero excess the SETTLED top lands
-- exactly on the DESIGN top, absolute error zero, which is what makes every
-- later metre attributable to excess and nothing else. A reader told that
-- settling is an excess effect would tighten the excess and expect the gap to
-- close, and it would not.
--
-- VERIFICATION IS WORTH SEVENTY METRES OF CEMENT. Unverified annular cement
-- needs 100 m; logged, it needs 30. Five of nine swept lengths flip from fail
-- to pass on the log alone. That is the Associate tier's rule about unverified
-- elements, priced.
--
-- WHAT THE PROGRAMME DOES NOT CHECK, STATED PLAINLY RATHER THAN DISCOVERED
-- LATER. The secondary barrier test asks only that a plug sits entirely above
-- the source top and passes the length rule. It does NOT test formation
-- competence or annular isolation behind the secondary, which the standard
-- does require, and annularBarrierCheck is a SEPARATE function that
-- abandonmentProgram never calls, so the 30 m and 100 m figures play no part
-- in a zone verdict at all. The engine header documents exactly this, so it is
-- a stated scope limit rather than a defect, and m05 l04 teaches it as one: a
-- passing programme is not a complete one.
--
-- The rules follow the commonly cited NORSOK D-010 rev 4 conventions, the
-- defaults are overridable, and the standard document governs. Literature
-- gate L19 is armed against the owner's copy.
-- ============================================================================

values ('integrity', 'advanced', '{"modules":[{"key":"m01-the-balanced-plug","title":"The Balanced Plug","lesson_keys":["l01-what-balanced-means","l02-the-four-capacities","l03-spacer-ahead-and-behind","l04-the-displacement"]},{"key":"m02-excess-and-where-the-plug-ends-up","title":"Excess, and Where the Plug Ends Up","lesson_keys":["l01-why-excess-at-all","l02-the-as-pumped-top","l03-pulling-the-stinger","l04-the-identity-at-zero-excess","l05-a-pump-chart-is-not-a-plug-top"]},{"key":"m03-the-rules","title":"The Rules","lesson_keys":["l01-a-hundred-metres-or-fifty","l02-what-a-foundation-buys","l03-above-the-source","l04-covering-the-source","l05-the-surface-plug"]},{"key":"m04-annular-cement","title":"Annular Cement","lesson_keys":["l01-the-barrier-outside-the-pipe","l02-thirty-metres-or-a-hundred","l03-what-a-log-buys","l04-verification-is-the-whole-difference"]},{"key":"m05-the-programme","title":"The Programme","lesson_keys":["l01-every-flowing-zone-needs-two","l02-primary-qualifying","l03-secondary-qualifying","l04-what-the-rule-does-not-check","l05-the-takeoff"]},{"key":"m06-the-expert-reading","title":"The Expert Reading","lesson_keys":["l01-the-story-so-far","l02-working-the-capstone","l03-onward"]}]}'::jsonb, 1)
